title: 'archive: $task->save dies on ref-backed tasks (Path::Tiny undef file_path)'
updated: 2026-07-02T02:03:51Z
---

REPRO
  karr archive <ID>   # on a board where tasks live in refs/karr/tasks/*, not on-disk files

  => Path::Tiny paths require defined, positive-length parts at App/karr/Task.pm line 122 (sub save)
The task IS moved to archived only if you fall back to `karr move <ID> archived`, which works.

ROOT CAUSE
Cmd/Archive.pm line 66 calls `$task->save;` directly (no $dir arg).
Task::save then hits the else branch: `path($self->file_path)`. For ref-backed
tasks, file_path is never set (from_file is not used; tasks come from the git
ref via find_task), so file_path is undef -> path(undef) dies in Path::Tiny.

Archive.pm is the ONLY Cmd that calls `$task->save`. Every other mutating Cmd
(Move, Edit, Pick, Handoff, Create) goes through the BoardAccess role method
`$self->save_task($task)`, which persists via BoardStore/Git (the ref backend)
and does not touch file_path. That is why `karr move ID archived` succeeds but
`karr archive ID` fails.

FIX (one line)
Cmd/Archive.pm:66  ->  replace `$task->save;` with `$self->save_task($task);`
(mirrors Move.pm:120 etc.)

FOLLOW-UP (optional hardening)
Task::save at Task.pm:143-149 blindly does path($self->file_path) when no $dir is
given. Consider die-with-clear-message or predicate guard (has_file_path) so a
missing file_path never surfaces as an opaque Path::Tiny error.

